## How to calculate some of the most important KPIs

Here are practical formulas you can use in a dashboard.

| KPI                     | Formula                                                        |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| SLA Compliance          | Requests completed within SLA ÷ Total completed requests × 100 |
| Contract Cycle Time     | Total days from request to signature ÷ Contracts signed        |
| Budget Variance         | (Actual spend − Budget) ÷ Budget × 100                         |
| Repository Completeness | Contracts with all required metadata ÷ Total contracts × 100   |
| Automation Rate         | Automated eligible workflows ÷ Total eligible workflows × 100  |
| AI Adoption             | Eligible workflows using AI ÷ Total eligible workflows × 100   |
| Project Delivery        | Projects delivered on time ÷ Total projects completed × 100    |

Important: Define the start and end points consistently. For example, contract cycle time can be measured from initial request to signature, or from Legal assignment to Legal approval. Those are different metrics.

## What I would prioritize for a fintech or crypto Legal Department

For a company with complex regulatory requirements, high contract volume, significant external counsel spend, and AI adoption initiatives, I would prioritize:

1. Legal Spend vs. Budget
2. Budget Forecast Accuracy
3. Contract Cycle Time
4. Contract Backlog
5. SLA Compliance
6. Regulatory Milestone Completion
7. Vendor Performance
8. AI Adoption Rate
9. Time Saved Through Automation
10. Internal Client Satisfaction

These give leadership visibility into cost, speed, risk, scalability, and business support.

One final recommendation: Every KPI should have an owner, a data source, a reporting frequency, a baseline, and a target. Otherwise, it becomes just a number on a dashboard rather than a management tool.

